{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792776800,"nonce":"QVt05bWRq6hVEZOSlyIjihP/VFI=","title":"LLVM OSR entries take seconds each and fill the single promoter for the whole run on a physics-heavy program","message":"ChimpMonk's CrowdGc (chimpmonk example/src/CrowdGc.hx, headless: a world of 256 boxes plus 8 skinned figures stepped at 60 Hz, `--scale 1`), native hybrid on the NUC (4 pinned cores, ash db4ea1df, machine loaded by another build, so absolute numbers are rough).\n\nASH_PROFILE=all over a 15 to 20 s run: the promoter thread spends 16.4 to 18.1 s of the run in \"llvm osr entry\" (84 percent of wall), 21 to 31 calls, of which \"llvm middle-end (osr)\" is 9.4 to 11.4 s (16 to 23 calls, so about 0.5 s each) and the rest, 5.7 to 7.5 s, is AIR to LLVM, codegen and module setup. Promotes (the functions themselves) are 0.8 s. Installs show the cost per function: JsonParser.parseRec 1.4 s, ConvexHull.triangles 4.2 s, ManifoldClipper.buildTopology 1.9 s, so the physics functions reach LLVM only after 6 to 8 s and run in Cranelift meanwhile.\n\nSwitching the middle end to default\u003cO1\u003e (ASH_LLVM_PASSES) cut the OSR middle-end from 11.4 to 9.4 s and frames in 15 s went from 445 to 588 on a noisy box; the O1 run spent more in the non-middle-end part (7.5 s), so the cost is not only the pass pipeline.\n\nFrames: every frame is over 16.6 ms at 1x in every mode tried (jit llvm-only, jit cranelift-only, hybrid), so the step itself is compute-bound; this issue is about time-to-LLVM, not the steady state.\n\nNot known: whether the large entries are needed (a Cranelift OSR entry already exists for the same loops), how big the AIR is for the slow ones, and what the steady-state step costs on an unloaded machine.\n\nIdeas, none tried: skip or defer the LLVM OSR entry for functions whose AIR is above a size, compile entries in hotness order, drop the duplicated callee bodies the entry module carries, and measure on an unloaded NUC (perf_event_paranoid is 4 after the reboot, so the sampler in ASH_PROFILE is the available profiler).","files":null}]}